  "title": "Kirby Problem 2.10",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "(a) Is there an efficient algorithm to compute distances in the curve complex\nof a surface? The input to the algorithm should be the surface and the\ncurves. One may ask similar questions for related complexes, such as the\narc complex of a surface with boundary.\n(b) Is there an algorithm (efficient or otherwise) to compute the distance be-\ntween quasi-convex subsets of the curve complex? This question is partic-\nularly interesting in the case where the quasi-convex subsets are the disk\nsets of handlebodies.",
